# Staging is the wrinkle — the same shape it takes for bracemark-web (see
# docs/env-files.md): a staging build is a PRODUCTION-mode build (NODE_ENV=
# production), so Expo won't auto-select this file by mode the way it does
# `.env.development` / `.env.production`. And we don't use EAS (no eas.json, and
# none is needed — builds are local), so there's no build profile to select it
# either: a staging build supplies the var inline
# (`EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=… expo export`), which takes precedence over
# `.env.production`. This file is the single source of those values to paste
# from. EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined at build time; nothing secret belongs here.
#
# Staging is its OWN registrable domain (dryrunbase.com), not a subdomain of
# bracemark.com — see docs/hosting.md, _why staging is a separate domain_.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.dryrunbase.com
# The marketing site's origin (bracemark-site), for out-of-app pages the mobile
# app links to (Support). NOT the bracemark-web app's origin — those pages live on
# the apex. Same staging-selection wrinkle as EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL above.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://dryrunbase.com
